in a bicategory \mbox{B}\hspace{1.0pt} requires a unit 2-morphism \mathbb {1}_{\mathtt {i}} \Rightarrow \mathrm {G}\circ \mathrm {F} and a counit 2-morphism \mathrm {F \circ G} \Rightarrow \mathbb {1}_{\mathtt {j}}. In particular, this axiomatization of adjointness explicitly requires the presence of unit 1-morphisms.In contrast to this, from , we know that unitality of a monoidal categority is a property, and not an additional structure: the unit object of a monoidal category is unique up to a unique isomorphism.

