Algorithm REF is an FWER-controlling algorithm; i.e., it satisfies Definition REF .The choices of the graph {{formula:66e4b25d-3fb3-4b93-b336-b8da06a66256}} and initial error budget {{formula:42f71599-07ec-423b-ae63-e10fb896b406}} are critical for the power of the procedure.
We next outline some basic principles guiding the design of these two parameters; see  for further discussion.
The general idea is that we want the error budget to be initially concentrated on a small number of hypotheses most likely to reject.
If these promising hypotheses are indeed rejected, then the error budget should flow to the next most promising set of hypotheses.
In this way, we proceed roughly from most promising hypotheses to least promising hypotheses, so that each test can be conducted at as a large of a significance level as possible, while giving the algorithm a chance to eventually visit all hypotheses.

