The HIdden COmmunity DEtection (HICODE) algorithm takes in a base algorithm {{formula:d8196d51-a728-4fff-9d1a-93fbcc79e2ca}} that finds one disjoint partition of communities A set of lightly overlapping communities is also allowed for the base algorithm {{formula:9262d89c-a51f-4077-b9c6-d5d5a7bc6404}} . Here we only consider the partition case for simplicity. and uses {{formula:9aef65dc-aa91-4fac-9a72-4a323c10beb5}} to identify and refine layers of community partitions. In the identification stage, HICODE iterates the following two steps until reaching a preset number of layers:Identify: Run {{formula:6c10f094-1b38-41c5-a8a1-164d539082e7}} to find one disjoint partition of communities on network {{formula:fdf043d7-21e8-4c25-b7b5-60a9bef00227}} and consider the partition as one layer of communities, {{formula:20330201-3661-4e74-ae14-505e9d4811a5}} ;

Weaken: Approximate edges contributed by layer {{formula:e3073dae-6ad9-45f0-a294-fe0a8875e028}} on {{formula:3541a1ba-5dfe-418a-a402-cd0df0939c91}} and reduce these edges on {{formula:399b6b20-2ed4-48ac-82e3-91476a18905d}} .HICODE then refines community partitions on each layer through iterating:Weaken: Approximate edges contributed by all layers except {{formula:9b2469e0-ee8c-4aab-ada8-1383075def99}} and reduce these edges on the original network {{formula:aed77c20-939c-472f-86dd-bc7835e633b1}} ;

Refine: Run {{formula:e40f5995-983e-4986-af4e-fac72702d30a}} on the remaining network to obtain a refined community partition for layer {{formula:1e996101-fb19-4d9e-a39d-c870102ebac2}} .

